---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_270",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 270,
  "text": "[[1044.8]] <b>222₅.  Demonstratio brevior DEMONSTRATIO BREVIOR\n[[1044.12]] <b>Demonstratio pure analytica</b>\n [[1044.13]] <b>Quod</b> <b>multiplicando minus per minus, producatur plus</b>,\n [[1044.14]] <b>seu</b> ─ <i>b</i> <b>in</b> ─ <i>c</i> <b>facit</b> + <i>bc</i> </p>\n<p> [[1044.15]] Suppono autem + in + facere +; et + in ─ facere ─. Item suppono regulas aequalitatum,\n[[1044.16]] caeteraque in calculo usitata, quae regulam hoc loco demonstrandam nondum\n[[1044.17]] requirunt.\n[[1045.1]] Propositio I\n [[1045.2]] ^&.bb <Leibniz special character><tab/>ut fiat <tab/>ducenda in <tab/>+ <i>fx</i> <tab/>─ <i>cx</i> <tab/>─ <i>b</i> <tab/> <tab/><i>aequ.</i> 0^&.b</i> <Leibniz special character> <tab/>Sit <tab/> + <i>x</i> <tab/>─ <i>b</i> <tab/><i>aequ. 0</i>\n [[1045.3]] <tab/>in <tab/> + <i>f</i> <tab/>─ <i>c</i>\n [[1045.4]] <tab/><picture>302</picture> <tab/>^#6+─ <i>cx</i> <tab/> · <greek>U</greek> ^#6- <tab/><picture>202</picture>\n [[1045.5]] <tab/>ut fiat <tab/><i>aequ. 0</i>\n [[1045.6]] <tab/>+ <i>fx</i> <tab/>─ <i>bf</i>\n [[1045.7]] posita <i>x</i> aequ. <i>b</i>\n [[1045.8]] ajo esse <greek>U</greek> aequ. + <i>bc</i>.\n[[1045.9]] Demonstratio </p>\n<p> [[1045.10]] Nam quia <i>x</i> aequ. <i>b</i>, erit <i>x</i> ─ <i>b</i> aequ. <i>0</i>, ergo <i>x</i> ─ <i>b</i> in <i>f</i> ─ <i>c</i> dabit <i>0</i> (quia, si <i>nihilo</i>\n[[1045.11]] aequale, ducatur in quidvis, productum erit <i>nihilo</i> aequale). Est autem <i>x</i> ─ <i>b</i> in <i>f</i> ─ <i>c</i> idem\n[[1045.12]] quod + <i>fx</i> ─ <i>cx</i> ─ <i>bf</i> · <greek>U</greek>, ut ostendimus; ergo fiet + <i>fx</i> ─ <i>cx</i> ─ <i>bf</i> · <greek>U</greek> aequ. <i>0</i>, seu, quod idem\n[[1045.13]] est, fiet · <greek>U</greek> aequ. + <i>cx</i> + <i>bf</i> ─ <i>fx</i>. </p>\n<p> [[1045.14]] Rursus quia <i>x</i> aequ. <i>b</i>\n [[1045.15]] hinc fiet <tab/>+ <i>fx aequ.</i> + <i>bf</i>\n [[1045.16]] item fiet <tab/>+ <i>bc aequ.</i> + <i>cx</i>\n [[1045.17]] Ergo aequalibus addendo aequalia, fiet + <i>fx</i> + <i>bc aequ. cx</i> + <i>bf</i>. Ergo + <i>bc</i> aequ. + <i>cx</i> + <i>bf</i> ─ <i>fx</i>.\n[[1045.18]] Sed paulo ante <greek>U</greek> erat etiam aequ. + <i>cx</i> + <i>bf</i> ─ <i>fx</i>, ergo erit <greek>U</greek> aequ. + <i>bc</i>\n[[1045.19]] quod demonstrandum proponebatur.\n[[1045.20]] Propositio II\n [[1045.21]] <tab/>Sit <tab/> + <i>d</i> <tab/>─ <i>b</i>\n [[1045.22]] <tab/>ducenda in <tab/> + <i>f</i> <tab/>─ <i>c</i>\n [[1045.23]] <tab/><picture>302</picture> <tab/>^#6+ <tab/>─ <i>cd</i> <tab/> · <greek>U</greek> ^#6-\n [[1045.24]] <tab/>ut fiat\n [[1045.25]] <tab/>+ <i>df</i> <tab/>─ <i>bf</i>\n [[1045.26]] Ajo (generaliter) esse <greek>U</greek> aequ. + <i>bc</i>.\n[[1045.27]] Demonstratio: </p>\n<p> [[1045.28]] Ponatur <i>d</i> aequ. + <i>e</i> + <i>x</i>, posito <i>b</i> aequ. <i>x</i>, et <i>e</i> existente excessu ipsius <i>d</i> supra <i>x</i> seu\n[[1045.29]] supra <i>b</i>, ergo + <i>d</i> ─ <i>b</i> idem erit quod + <i>e</i> + <i>x</i> ─ <i>b</i>, Ergo + <i>d</i> ─ <i>b</i> in <i>f</i> ─ <i>c</i> idem erit quod\n[[1046.1]] + <i>e</i> + <i>x</i> ─ <i>b</i> in <i>f</i> ─ <i>c</i>. Jam + <i>e</i> in <i>f</i> ─ <i>c</i> est + <i>ef</i> ─ <i>ce</i>, et + <i>x</i> ─ <i>b</i> in + <i>f</i> ─ <i>c</i> (: posito scil. hic\n[[1046.2]] <i>x</i> aequ. <i>b</i> :) est + <i>fx</i> ─ <i>cx</i> ─ <i>bf</i> + <i>bc</i> per prop. I. Ergo (duo producta in unum colligendo)\n[[1046.3]] + <i>e</i> + <i>x</i> ─ <i>b</i> in + <i>f</i> ─ <i>c</i>, seu + <i>d</i> ─ <i>b</i> in + <i>f</i> ─ <i>c</i> erit: + <i>ef</i> ─ <i>ce</i>, + <i>fx</i> ─ <i>cx</i> ─ <i>bf</i> + <i>bc</i>. At supra\n[[1046.4]] + <i>d</i> ─ <i>b</i> in + <i>f</i> ─ <i>c</i>, erat aequ. + <i>df</i> ─ <i>cd</i> ─ <i>bf</i> · <greek>U</greek>.\n [[1046.5]] Ergo hos duos valores aequando et tollendo utrobique, ─ <i>bf</i>, fiet:\n [[1046.6]] (+ <i>ef</i> ─ <i>ce</i> + <i>fx</i> ─ <i>cx</i> + <i>bc aequ. df</i> ─ <i>cd</i> · <greek>U</greek>).\n [[1046.7]] Est autem + <i>ef</i> + <i>fx</i> aequ. + <i>df</i> et ─ <i>ce</i> ─ <i>cx</i> aequ. ─ <i>cd</i>, quia <i>d</i> aequ. <i>e</i> + <i>x</i>. </p>\n<p> [[1046.8]] Ergo + <i>ef</i> ─ <i>ce</i> + <i>fx</i> ─ <i>cx</i> aequ. <i>df</i> ─ <i>cd</i>. Ergo si in priori aequatione\n [[1046.9]] (<tab/>+ <i>ef</i> ─ <i>ce</i> + <i>fx</i> ─ <i>cx</i> + <i>bc aequ.</i> <tab/>+ <i>df</i> ─ <i>cd</i> · <greek>U</greek>)\n [[1046.10]] <tab/><kuo8> <tab/><kuo3>\n [[1046.11]] tollantur utrinque aequalia, restabit <greek>U</greek> <i>aequ.</i> + <i>bc</i>.\n [[1046.12]] Quod erat demonstrandum.\n[[1046.13]] Scholion </p>\n<p> [[1046.14]] Renaldinus aliique qui calculi regulas demonstrare voluere, usi sunt propositionibus\n[[1046.15]] Euclidis lib. 2. <i>Elementorum</i>, ad probandum quod ─ in ─ facit +. Unde Mariottus in\n[[1046.16]] Specimine Logico, negat eas propositiones geometricas per calculum probari posse, fieri\n[[1046.17]] enim circulum. Sed quoniam hinc sequeretur vulgarissimas Arithmeticae operationes (ex\n[[1046.18]] quibus est ista operatio per + et ─) pendere a propositionibus geometricis et linearum\n[[1046.19]] ductu, quod minime rationi consentaneum est; hinc modum quaesivi demonstrandi regulam\n[[1046.20]] quod ─ in ─ facit + per purum calculum, quem vel in numeris vel in lineis interpretari\n[[1046.21]] licet. Idque mihi Cavalerius quoque optasse videtur, quando hujus Algorithmi demonstrationem\n[[1046.22]] desiderabat Renaldino teste. Nam linearem demonstrationem apud Algebristas, ut\n[[1046.23]] Bombellum aliosque extare, non poterat ignorare. </p>\n",
  "number": "222₅.",
  "title": "Demonstratio brevior",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:222₅. Demonstratio brevior DEMONSTRATIO BREVIOR Demonstratio pure analytica Quod multiplicando minus per minus, producatur plus, seu ─ b in ─ c facit + bc Suppono autem + in + facere +; et + in ─ facere ─. Item suppono regulas aequalitatum, caeteraque in calculo usitata, quae regulam hoc loco demons...">
      <div class="text-content">
        {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
          paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>